.TH "S3AR\-PUT" "1" "September 2026" "s3ar" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
s3ar\-put \- upload a file or standard input to an S3 object
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
s3ar\-put [\-v|\-vv|\-vvv] [\-f FILE] [\-\-create\-bucket] [\-\-multipart\-size SIZE] s3://BUCKET/KEY
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]\f[CB]s3ar\-put\f[B]\f[R] reads data from standard input, or from
\f[I]\f[CI]FILE\f[I]\f[R] when \f[B]\f[CB]\-f\f[B]\f[R] is specified, and writes
it to the selected S3 object.
Objects up to the selected part size, inclusive, use a single PUT; larger
objects use multipart upload.
The default part size and threshold are 16M.
Only one part plus one byte of lookahead is buffered at a time.
The command reads this initial data before starting the upload, including when
reading standard input.
An upload is limited to 10,000 parts; if the input exceeds that limit for the
selected part size, the upload fails and its multipart state is aborted.
Successful uploads are reported on standard error, even without
\f[B]\f[CB]\-v.\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-f \-\f[B]\f[R] selects standard input explicitly.
.PP
The operand names exactly one object; an existing object with that key is
overwritten.
KEY is literal, not URL\-decoded, and a trailing slash is part of the key.
Quote operands containing spaces or shell metacharacters.
.SH OPTIONS
\f[B]\f[CB]\-f FILE, \-\-file=FILE\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Read data from FILE instead of standard input.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-create\-bucket\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Check the destination bucket before uploading and create it if it is missing,
using the configured S3 region.
Existing buckets are used without modification.
Other errors, including access denied, stop the command.
Without this option, the destination bucket must already exist.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-\-multipart\-size SIZE\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Set the multipart part size and the threshold for a single PUT.
Objects up to SIZE, inclusive, use a single PUT.
SIZE must be between 5M and 5G, inclusive.
The upload buffer uses up to SIZE bytes plus one byte of lookahead.
Only the binary suffixes M (1024 squared bytes) and G (1024 cubed bytes) are
accepted.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-v, \-\-verbose\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Increase verbosity.
One occurrence selects informational messages; two select debug messages; three
select HTTP trace.
Further occurrences have no effect.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]\-h, \-\-help\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Display command usage on standard output and exit successfully.
.SH EXAMPLES
Upload a local file:
.IP
.EX
s3ar\-put \-f original.jpg s3://photos/original.jpg
.EE
.PP
Upload standard input:
.IP
.EX
cat original.jpg | s3ar\-put s3://photos/original.jpg
.EE
.PP
Create the destination bucket if necessary and use 64M multipart parts:
.IP
.EX
s3ar\-put \-\-create\-bucket \-\-multipart\-size 64M \-f backup.tar s3://backups/backup.tar
.EE
.SH SIGNALS
\f[B]\f[CB]SIGUSR1\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Increase diagnostic verbosity by one level, up to trace.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]SIGUSR2\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
Decrease diagnostic verbosity by one level, down to fatal.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
\f[B]\f[CB]S3AR_ENDPOINT,\f[B]\f[R] \f[B]\f[CB]S3AR_REGION,\f[B]\f[R]
\f[B]\f[CB]S3AR_URI_STYLE,\f[B]\f[R] \f[B]\f[CB]S3AR_ACCESS_KEY,\f[B]\f[R]
\f[B]\f[CB]S3AR_SECRET_KEY,\f[B]\f[R] and
\f[B]\f[CB]S3AR_SESSION_TOKEN\f[B]\f[R] configure the S3 connection in the same
way as for \f[B]\f[CB]s3ar(1).\f[B]\f[R]
.SH EXIT STATUS
\f[B]\f[CB]0\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
The upload or help completed successfully.
.PP
\f[B]\f[CB]2\f[B]\f[R]
.PP
A fatal error occurred, including an invalid command line, S3 configuration,
bucket check or creation failure, upload failure, or input\-file failure.
.PP
When an S3 operation fails after a retry, the diagnostic includes the number of
attempts.
